  "prompt_text": "The figure compares present and possible future working conditions across three settings—outdoor agriculture, indoor factory work, and indoor office work—under rising heat. In the historical row, work proceeds normally with moderate temperatures. In the future scenario without labour adaptation, thermometers and worker icons suggest hotter conditions reduce labour capacity across all settings. Outdoors, crop trees appear stressed and some workers are absent or replaced by equipment, while factory and office scenes show fewer active workers despite cooling units being present.\n\nThe bottom row shows a future with labour adaptation, emphasizing that productivity losses can be reduced through a mix of responses tailored to each workplace. Outdoors, visible measures include shifted work timing, mechanization, shade, lighter clothing, breaks, and warning systems. In factories and offices, the buildings appear upgraded with stronger cooling and structural protections, and icons indicate strategies such as air conditioning, insulation, regulations, and altered schedules. The overall message is that climate warming threatens labour performance in many sectors, but a portfolio of behavioural, organizational, and technological adaptations can help workers continue operating more safely and effectively.",
